WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.582
Welcome to Module 11, Advanced Pandas.

00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:10.607
In the previous module, we worked with the basic building blocks of a DataFrame: selecting columns, filtering rows,

00:00:10.607 --> 00:00:15.892
sorting values, and creating simple summaries.

00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:21.702
Now we are going to connect those skills into larger, more realistic workflows.

00:00:21.702 --> 00:00:26.667
The main idea is not to memorize a long list of Pandas functions.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:32.582
Instead, I want you to think about how a table changes from one step to the next.

00:00:32.582 --> 00:00:38.937
We may start with raw data, clean or transform it, reshape it when necessary, summarize it,

00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:46.453
check that our joins are correct, and then produce something that is ready for analysis or reporting.

00:00:47.061 --> 00:00:54.683
As you work through this module, keep asking yourself one question: what does this operation change in my data,

00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:57.163
and why do I need that change?

00:00:57.163 --> 00:01:02.903
That question will help you understand Pandas much better than memorizing syntax.

00:01:02.903 --> 00:01:09.233
We will work with a small order dataset throughout the module so you can focus on the logic.

00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:17.370
By the end, you should be able to build a complete Pandas workflow that is readable, reusable, and easier to validate.
